Let's analyze the method `set(int fromIndex, int toIndex, boolean value)` and the comment `// @@@ Every bit in the valid interval equals the supplied boolean value.`

This comment suggests that after calling `set(fromIndex, toIndex, value)`, every bit in the range `[fromIndex, toIndex)` should be equal to `value`.

To translate this into an assert statement, we need to check that for every index `i` in the range `[fromIndex, toIndex)`, `this.get(i)` equals `value`. We can use the `\forall` quantifier to express this.

The assert statement would look like this:

<code>assert \forall int i; fromIndex <= i && i < toIndex; this.get(i) == value;</code>
